  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: "A common fable told in bars speaks of a lion,
    king of old Aija. The Lion desired meat but also wanted potatoes. Not knowing
    what he wanted, he ordered his chefs to make something truly regal. The chefs
    all raced to the kitchen, eager to impress the Lion. The Cat baked the finest
    black bread. The Bull mashed the best taters. The Hawk too, assured the most
    tender loin. And then the Aphid, who did nay but mashed his peers\u2019 work
    together and presented the bapka to the Lion. Only three pikes were shown outside
    the castle that day, the Aphid not among them."
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: There is nothing better in life than to make a meal
    with great pride. Bapka are great examples, being works of art by themselves.
    But passion can take its toll on even the finest artist, dulling their colors,
    their might. What love is there when the bread is filled with a void as black
    as the Aijinkovan soil? <i>All twenty thousand kilometers left to toil.</i>
